<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
	Unrefined magicyte (RawMagicyte) ends up in two thing categories: TM_Magicyte ("refined
	magicyte") inherited from its abstract parent MagicResourceBase_Magicyte, plus TM_MagicItems
	from its own def, because list nodes merge with the parent's by default. TM_Magicyte is
	itself a child of TM_MagicItems, so the item appears twice in the category tree.

	The game's real wealth (WealthWatcher) counts each thing once, so this is harmless there,
	but anything that walks the category tree lists it twice - notably Visible Wealth, whose
	item breakdown builds one node per (category, thingDef) and sums them, so the Items and
	Magic Items totals include all raw magicyte twice. It also files the raw stone under
	"refined magicyte".

	Fix: keep only TM_MagicItems. A plain PatchOperationRemove can't do it - the inherited
	TM_Magicyte entry isn't in RawMagicyte's XML when patches run (inheritance resolves
	afterwards) - so the whole list is replaced with Inherit="False" to stop the merge.
	No RWoM recipe or filter references the TM_Magicyte category for raw magicyte.
-->
<Patch>

	<Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
		<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName = "RawMagicyte"]/thingCategories</xpath>
		<value>
			<thingCategories Inherit="False">
				<li>TM_MagicItems</li>
			</thingCategories>
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
